verdict.reason:
Reproduced on my own stubs (test STUBS plus Becoming/Probe.lean), running the check at ffccb515d and at 36d4b0fae on the same oleans. Script: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ren-theories/4cd2c9b9-8aca-4fd1-99bb-ff1a3f9d1698/scratchpad/recheck-refute-regressions/stubs.py; output: stubs-out.json in the same folder. Each of these recoveries is by definitions alone and certified by rfl, and each now fails test 9, though every one passes at 36d4b0fae:
- a well-founded `Model.half` (decreasing_by omega) with recovery `total_form (fun x => ⟨Model.half x, rfl⟩)` gives 'the recovery uses [Becoming.Model.half._proof_1]';
- `deriving DecidableEq` reached through an `if` gives `instDecidableEqTone._proof_1/_2`;
- `Model.three : Fin 3 := ⟨2, by decide⟩` gives `Model.three._proof_1`.
Structural recursion still passes, and the base test entry is unchanged. The mechanism is in theoremsUsed (boundary_check.lean:209-213). namesOf includes the declaration's type, so the walk enters every package definition the row's statement or the recovery names. Lean puts termination, decide and structure-field proofs into package `_proof_N` theorems, and isProof then collects them. LEAN-1's verifier asked for exactly the opposite: 'so termination or decide proofs raise no spurious use'. The spec's test 9 (BOUNDARY-FIELD.md §3.2: 'its termination lemmas, say, are not counted') and the docstring at lines 193-196 promise the same. Neither holds, because the Init exemption never reaches a `_proof_N` theorem: it is collected, not entered. On GW's dump, the emulation in gw_walk.py (same folder) finds that 19 of the 118 central rows' statements alone reach a package theorem through package definitions. 13 of them reach `Becoming.Law.run._proof_1`, whose dump body names only `Law.orbit`. So no recovery stating those rows could pass test 9. GW's dump also holds 335 `instDecidableEq*._proof_N` theorems. U4's rows 17 and 5 reach none of these, which is why the controls are unchanged. The check fails closed, so nothing is accepted wrongly, but valid entries for about one central row in six are refused with a misleading reason, and no test covers it.
